title: Authorizations › Queue › Bands and ranking
route: /authorizations
intro: How open requests are split into three bands, when a request leaves its band, how they are ranked inside a band by how soon each is due, and how a band opens, closes and shows more.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: which band a request sits in is fixed in the seed data. Moving the demo clock changes the due text on each tile ('in 5 h', 'now') but never moves a request to another band.
---
screen q "Queue\nPriority bands, most urgent first"
process b1 "Each open request at the sites in view sits in exactly one band\nBand counts for Both sites are the Site A counts plus the Site B counts"
process lv "A request leaves its band once nothing is left for a person\nPreparing or ready: it was signed and sent in New case\nWith the payer: the payer approved or denied it\nDenial route: accepted, settled on the call, or the appeal is filed"

group gB "Three bands"
  process bn "**Act now**\nRed dot, tiles tinted red"
  process bd "**Due within 24 hours**\nAmber dot"
  process bw "**Due this week**\nSage dot"
endgroup

decision dE "Does the band have any request after filters?"
decision dZ "Is it Act now, with no request open at all, and no search, payer or status filter on?"
screen em "Band card stays\n'Act now (0 requests)'\n'Nothing needs you today'\n'Everything in Act now has been sent or handled.'\nWith one site in view: 'No open request at Site B is in Act now.'"
process hide "The band card is left out"
screen bc "Band card\n'Act now (5 requests)'\nName, count, chevron"

process r1 "Inside a band, requests waiting on a person come first\nPreparing, Ready to sign, Denial route, or Needs your input"
process r2 "Then the soonest due first\nThe due time on the tile, earliest at the top"
process wt "Two due at the same time\nThe lower approval chance goes first"
doc ex "Example in Act now\nR-1117 (due in 30 h, needs you) ranks above R-0912 (due in 22 h, payer already reviewing)"

click hd "Click the band header"
decision dC "Is the band open now?"
process col "Tiles are hidden\nChevron turns sideways"
process exp "Tiles are shown\nChevron points down"
store keep "Open or closed is remembered for each band\nuntil the demo data is reset"

decision dM "More than five requests in the band?"
process all5 "All requests are shown"
process top5 "Top five are shown\nButton under them: 'Show 9 more'"
click sm "Click 'Show 9 more'"
process allm "Every request is shown\nButton now reads 'Show fewer'"
click sf "Click 'Show fewer'"
process back "Back to the top five"

click tp "Hover or focus the info icon 'How the list is ordered' (right end of the filter bar)"
overlay tp2 "Tooltip says the same rule in a few words\nEsc closes it"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Queue › Read and open a request row"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Queue › Sites: what each viewer sees"

q --> b1
b1 --> lv
b1 -.-> g2
b1 --> bn & bd & bw
bn --> dE
bd --> dE
bw --> dE
dE -->|No| dZ
dZ -->|Yes| em
dZ -->|No| hide
dE -->|Yes| bc
bc --> r1 --> r2 --> wt
r2 -.-> ex
r1 --> tp --> tp2
bc --> hd --> dC
dC -->|Yes| col --> keep
dC -->|No| exp --> keep
bc --> dM
dM -->|No| all5
dM -->|Yes| top5 --> sm --> allm --> sf --> back
top5 --> g1
